hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16750","Abu Salih al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: my father informed us, from his father, from Dhu al-Jawshan al-Dibabi, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he had finished with the people of Badr, with the son of a mare of mine called al-Qarha, and said: O Muhammad, I have brought you the son of al-Qarha to take it; he said: I have no need of it, and if you wish that I compensate you in it with the choicest of the armors of Badr, I will do; I said: I would not compensate it today for a load; he said: I have no need of it; then he said: O Dhu al-Jawshan, will you not submit, to be among the first of the people of this matter; I said: No; he said: Why; I said: I saw your people enamored of you; he said: Then how did it reach you of their deaths at Badr; I said: It reached me; he said: Then we guide for you; I said: If you overcome the Kaba and settle it; he said: Perhaps if you live you will see that; then he said: O Bilal, take the bag of the man and provision him from ajwa; when I turned away he said: He is indeed among the best horsemen of Banu Amir; he said: By Allah, I was with my family in al-Ghawr when a rider came; I said: What did the people do; he said: By Allah, Muhammad has overcome the Kaba and settled it; I said: May my mother mourn me, had I submitted then and asked him for al-Hira he would have granted it to me."
"16751","Shayban ibn Abi Shayba Abu Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, he said: Dhu al-Jawshan came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and gifted him a horse, while he was then a polytheist, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused to accept it, then said: If you wish, sell it to me, or do you wish to sell it to me for the choicest of the armors of Badr; then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you wish to be the first to enter this matter; he said: No; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What prevents you from that; he said: I saw your people deny you and expel you and fight you, so see what you do; if you prevail over them I will believe in you and follow you, and if they prevail over you I will not follow you; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Dhu al-Jawshan, perhaps if you remain, and he mentioned the hadith much like it."
"16752","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Dhu al-Jawshan, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he had finished with Badr, with the son of a mare of mine called al-Qarha, and said: O Muhammad, and he mentioned the hadith."
